After looking at these three models, transformers are a good way to attack language modeling because of attention. The bigram can only see one character, and the LSTM can only pass its memory onto one character at a time. A transformer allows every character to look at the early ones and make a decision on whether they matter, so it can use this as context without relying on a large memory. It also has the ability to process everything at once, which is most likely more beneficial for large datasets. For my test, the LSTM had the lowest validation loss, but the transformer's loss continued to fall when training stopped. This could be helped by more data and training.
